      "id": "focus",
      "kind": "proof",
      "title": "Induction proof of the sum of positive integers",
      "text": "The base case and the induction step together establish the finite sum formula for positive integers.",
      "refs": [
        {
          "document_id": "lesson",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "document_id": "lesson",
          "page": 2
        }
      ],
      "details": {
        "academic": {
          "nature": "derivation",
          "assumptions": [
            "n is a positive integer"
          ],
          "steps": [
            {
              "text": "For n=1, S_1=1=1(1+1)/2. Assume S_k=k(k+1)/2.",
              "refs": [
                {
                  "document_id": "lesson",
                  "page": 1
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "S_(k+1)=k(k+1)/2+(k+1)=(k+1)(k+2)/2.",
              "refs": [
                {
                  "document_id": "lesson",
                  "page": 2
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q",
      "kind": "question",
      "title": "Practice problem",
      "text": "Original teaching exercise.\nUse mathematical induction to prove that for every positive integer n, S_n=1+2+...+n=n(n+1)/2. At n=1 both sides equal 1. Suppose that the formula holds for some integer k>=1.",
      "refs": [
        {
          "document_id": "lesson",
          "page": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "q-a",
      "kind": "question",
      "title": "Part a",
      "text": "Calculate the finite sum for n=10 and explain why the proof requires n to be a positive integer.",
      "refs": [
        {
          "document_id": "lesson",
          "page": 2
        }
      ],
      "parent_id": "q"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-a",
      "kind": "answer",
      "title": "Worked answer for the original practice exercise",
      "text": "S_10=55. The base case and successor step cover the positive integers. A non-integer count of terms lies outside the claim.",
      "refs": [
        {
          "document_id": "lesson",
          "page": 2
        }
